@startuml clip-processing
!include style.iuml
title Clip Processing: Inbox to Searchable Record

participant "Worker\nworker.py" as W
participant "Pipeline\npipeline.py" as P
participant "ffmpeg\nmedia.py" as FF
participant "Whisper\nstt.py" as S
participant "Faces\nfaces.py" as FA
participant "Laya\nlaya-serve :8000" as L
participant "Mood\nvibe.py" as V
participant "Indexer\nindexing.py" as I
database "Postgres\npgvector" as DB

== POLL ==
loop every POLL_SECONDS (3 s), for each settled file in data/inbox
  W -> W : sync_gallery_if_changed()
  note right of W
    **worker.py · sync_gallery_if_changed()**
    Re-reads data/gallery/<Person>/*.jpg only
    when a file changed; new photos re-match
    faces already seen in old clips.
  end note
  W -> W : pending()
  note right of W
    **worker.py · pending()**
    Video files in data/inbox untouched for
    more than 2 s (still copying otherwise),
    oldest first.
  end note
  W -> P : process_clip(conn, video)

== READ AND PROBE ==
P -> P : load_meta(sidecar)
note right of P
  **pipeline.py · load_meta()**
  clip.json (ours) or clip.info.json (yt-dlp).
  Adds: title, caption, language, hashtags,
  people, folk_names, topics, reactions ...
end note
P -> FF : probe(video)
FF --> P : duration, width, height, has_audio
alt duration > MAX_CLIP_SECONDS (30 s)
  P --> W : raise Rejected
  W -> W : move_aside(video, data/failed)
end

== DUPLICATES ==
P -> FF : sha256(video)
P -> DB : find_duplicate(sha)
alt same file already stored
  P -> DB : merge_duplicate()
  note right of P
    **pipeline.py · merge_duplicate()**
    duplicates_seen + 1 (the trend signal).
    The uploader's title and caption are kept
    as extra names people use for the meme.
  end note
  P --> W : status "duplicate", match "exact"
end
P -> FF : extract_keyframes(4) + dhash()
FF --> P : 4 jpg frames, 4 x 64-bit picture hashes
P -> DB : find_duplicate(sha, phash)
note right of DB
  Near duplicate when the mean Hamming
  distance <= DEDUP_MAX_HAMMING (6 of 64 bits)
  and durations differ < 0.7 s.
  Catches re-encodes and resizes.
end note
alt picture hashes close to a stored clip
  P -> DB : merge_duplicate()
  P --> W : status "duplicate", match "near"
end

== WEB COPY ==
P -> FF : transcode() + make_thumb()
FF --> P : media/<sha16>.mp4, media/<sha16>.jpg

== SPEECH ==
P -> FF : extract_audio()
P -> S : transcribe(wav, language="hi")
S --> P : text, avg_logprob, language_probability
note right of S
  **stt.py · transcribe()**
  faster-whisper "small", int8 on CPU.
  vad_filter skips music-only stretches.
  low_stt_confidence when avg_logprob < -1.0
  or language_probability < 0.5.
end note
P -> P : to_roman(native)
note right of P
  **text.py · to_roman()**
  Devanagari dialogue is also stored in
  Roman letters, so it is findable as
  "nam ya dam" (clip 6).
end note
P -> DB : INSERT INTO clips (facts so far)
DB --> P : clip_id

== PEOPLE ==
P -> DB : people_in_text(title, caption, hashtags)
P -> FA : detect(frame) x 4
FA --> P : 512-number face vectors + boxes
P -> DB : record_faces(clip_id, faces)
note right of FA
  **faces.py · record_faces()**
  Each face is matched against the gallery;
  cosine >= FACE_MATCH_THRESHOLD (0.42) names it.
  Flags: unknown_faces, weak_face_match.
end note

== TOPICS (LAYA) ==
P -> L : POST /v1/systemone\nstate: title + dialogue + people\nquestions: topic (choice), mood (choice)
L --> P : probability per topic and per mood
P -> L : POST /v1/systemone\nstate: title, caption, people only\nquestions: topic (choice)
L --> P : probability per topic
note right of L
  **laya.py · describe_clip()**
  One forward pass per call, no text generated.
  Asked twice because noisy transcripts pull the
  answer to generic topics; the title alone is
  sharp when it names the topic.
  A topic is kept at >= 0.45 in either reading
  (max 5), after any sidecar topics.
end note
P -> DB : UPDATE clips SET topics

== MOOD ==
P -> V : analyse(frames, faces, dialogue, laya_mood)
V -> V : face_scores(): FER+ on each face crop
V -> V : scene_scores(): CLIP keyframes vs 13 mood sentences
V -> V : combine() + pick()
note right of V
  **vibe.py · combine()**
  faces 0.45, scene 0.40, Laya text 0.30
  (weights re-scaled when a signal is missing).
  Moods >= VIBE_MIN_SCORE (0.30), top 3.
  use_when from a fixed table per mood,
  description from a template.
end note
V --> P : reactions, use_when, description, raw scores
P -> DB : UPDATE (only fields the sidecar left empty)

== INDEX ==
P -> DB : UPDATE people, needs_review, review_reasons, raw
P -> I : refresh(conn, clip_id)
I -> I : search_fields()
note right of I
  **indexing.py · search_fields()**
  s_names   folk names + cleaned title
  s_said    romanised transcript
  s_people  people + aliases + film
  s_meta    caption, mood, use-when, topics
  all through normalise(): the same function
  the query goes through at search time.
end note
I -> I : embed_one(embedding_text())
note right of I
  MiniLM multilingual -> 384 numbers.
  Text: title, dialogue, people, film,
  "Mood: ...", "Use when: ...", "About: ...".
end note
I -> DB : UPDATE s_* columns, embedding
P --> W : status "new", clip_id, review reasons
W -> W : move_aside(video, data/processed)
note right of W
  **worker.py · run_once()**
  Any exception: the original goes to
  data/failed with the traceback in
  <name>.error.txt; the loop carries on.
end note
end
@enduml
